Android's phone WebPreferences on an OHOS phone.

WebPreferences turns several touch-phone behaviours on by BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
rather than by device, so the OHOS phone got the Linux desktop's: no zoom
into a focused field on a zoomed-out page, -webkit-text-size-adjust ignored,
find-in-page jumping between matches, and desktop editing rules. Set them in
ApplyOhosPhoneWebPreferences, which only runs for the phone UI family.

A tablet, or an unfolded foldable in the large-screen UI, has a
touchscreen as well that Ozone OHOS does not report: maxTouchPoints read 0
and pages saw no touch events. Report it for device classes tablet and
phone (--ohos-device-class) outside the phone UI too, leaving the primary
pointer and hover as Chromium finds them.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-phone-android-web-prefs.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -4542,6 +4542,23 @@
                                   content::SiteInstance& main_frame_site,
                                   WebPreferences* web_prefs) {
   if (!chrome::ohos::IsAuraShellMobilePhoneUi()) {
+    // A tablet, or an unfolded foldable showing the large-screen UI, has a
+    // touchscreen too, and Ozone OHOS reports it no more than a phone's:
+    // maxTouchPoints read 0 and pages saw no touch events behind a window
+    // that is a tablet. --ohos-device-class says which devices have one (an
+    // unfolded foldable is still "phone"); a 2in1 may not, and keeps the
+    // desktop defaults. The primary pointer and hover stay as Chromium finds
+    // them, since a tablet with a keyboard and mouse attached still hovers.
+    // Not URL-dependent, so it never needs revisiting.
+    const std::string device_class =
+        base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->GetSwitchValueASCII(
+            "ohos-device-class");
+    if (device_class == "tablet" || device_class == "phone") {
+      web_prefs->touch_event_feature_detection_enabled = true;
+      web_prefs->pointer_events_max_touch_points = 10;
+      web_prefs->available_pointer_types |=
+          static_cast<int>(blink::mojom::PointerType::kPointerCoarseType);
+    }
     return false;
   }
 
@@ -4559,6 +4576,18 @@
   web_prefs->primary_hover_type = blink::mojom::HoverType::kHoverNone;
   web_prefs->default_maximum_page_scale_factor = 5.0f;
 
+  // What WebPreferences defaults to on Android and leaves off everywhere
+  // else, because it keys on the build rather than on the device: focusing a
+  // field on a zoomed-out page zooms in until its text is legible,
+  // -webkit-text-size-adjust is honoured, find-in-page scrolls to each match
+  // instead of jumping, and caret and selection editing follow Android's
+  // touch rules rather than a Linux desktop's.
+  web_prefs->auto_zoom_focused_editable_to_legible_scale = true;
+  web_prefs->text_size_adjust_enabled = true;
+  web_prefs->smooth_scroll_for_find_enabled = true;
+  web_prefs->editing_behavior =
+      blink::mojom::EditingBehavior::kEditingAndroidBehavior;
+
   // WebUI is written for a desktop window and almost none of it declares a
   // <meta viewport>: 29 files in all of chrome/browser/resources do, and
   // password_manager.html is not one. Under the mobile rules it would be laid
